    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d646">

                <pb facs="0697" n="685" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg685"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Brazil/752: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-06-23T22:00:00-04:00">June 23, 1942—10 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1639. Your 2157, June 22, 5 p.m. You are authorized to exchange notes with the
                    Foreign Office along the lines suggested.</p>
                <p>It is planned that rubber will not be handled through this purchasing commission.
                    A special arrangement is planned by the Board of Economic Warfare and the Rubber
                    Reserve Company<anchor n="7" xml:id="d646-f1"/> whereby Allen<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d646-f2"/> will be designated by both these Agencies as head of the
                    rubber program in Brazil. It is assumed that nothing in the proposed notes will
                    interfere with these arrangements.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d646-f1" n="7" xml:id="d646-f1-content">
                <p>The Rubber Reserve Company was a purchasing agency of the Department of
                    Commerce.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d646-f2" n="8" xml:id="d646-f2-content">
                <p>Douglas H. Allen, Special Assistant to the President of the Rubber Reserve
                    Company.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
